# build output
dist/
.astro/

# wrangler's local state: miniflare's sqlite caches and the bundles it writes
# while `wrangler dev` is running. Regenerated on every run, machine-specific,
# and nothing here is an input to a deploy — CI builds dist/ and uploads it.
.wrangler/

# dependencies
node_modules/

# generated — never commit, CI builds this from src/data/cv.json
public/resume.pdf

# Portfolio.pdf and the JSON it is built from. Ignored as a whole directory,
# and that is the entire privacy mechanism — see the header of
# src/resume/portfolio.typ.
#
# The site is a Worker with static assets and no `main`: no code runs on a
# request, so nothing can check who is asking, and every file under public/ is a
# public URL to anyone who knows it. A password in JavaScript is read out of the
# page source and an unguessable filename is not secrecy when the repo naming it
# is public.
# So this document is not published at all — built locally by `npm run
# portfolio`, never committed, never copied into dist/, never built in CI.
# Writing it anywhere under public/ would undo that in one line.
private/

# Raw hero renders: ~200 transparent PNGs at 2400px, about a gigabyte. The
# committed artefact is public/hero/, which `npm run hero` builds from these.
# They live under images/ with the other source artwork the site does not read.
images/hero-frames/

# Source résumé PDFs stay local: they carry a phone number and this repo may
# become public. Docs/Resume.MD (phone stripped) is the tracked source of truth.
Docs/*.pdf
!Docs/Portfolio_Architecture_Blueprint.pdf

# logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# environment
.env
.env.production

# editor / OS
.claude/settings.local.json
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Client and employer source artwork. This folder is where raw exports land,
# and several already in it are Altium 3D renders — every trace, via and
# reference designator, with silkscreen naming the client and the board
# revision. This repo is public, and the IP boundary in CLAUDE.md says those
# must never be committed; git history would keep them even after a delete.
#
# Ignored as a whole directory rather than file by file, because the failure
# mode is a new export dropped in here and swept up by the next `git add -A`.
# Nothing is lost: the site reads src/assets/, and what it publishes is
# committed there. `images/others/Maiman Studio Logo.jpg` predates this rule
# and stays tracked — ignoring a directory does not untrack what is already in.
images/others/
